<title>USA: USDA - Tennessee free of cattle disease brucellosis.</title>
<headline>USDA - Tennessee free of cattle disease brucellosis.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Agriculture Department Wednesday declared Tennessee free of the cattle disease brucellosis, relieving certain restrictions on the interstate movement of the state's 66,000 head of cattle.</p>
<p>The target date for eradicating the cattle disease from the United States is 1998.</p>
<p>Currently, all but 13 states are brucellosis free, USDA said.</p>
</text>
